  "answer": "Malicious File Upload is an attack mechanism categorized under injection attacks. It involves an attacker exploiting a vulnerability in a web application that allows them to upload files. If the application does not properly validate or restrict the types of files that can be uploaded, the attacker can upload a malicious file, which may then be executed on the server or used to compromise the application.\n\nThe attack is associated with CAPEC ID CAPEC-17 and MITRE ATT&CK ID T1190, indicating its relevance in public-facing application contexts. Proper prevention and mitigation strategies are outlined in the OWASP File Upload Cheat Sheet, which emphasizes the importance of validating file types and implementing strict controls on file uploads to prevent such attacks [Source 1][Source 2].",
